Each arm runs in a SEPARATE INTERPRETER. Patching the derivation in-process and
analysing twice shares every module-level cache the analyzer holds, which is how
a run reports the first arm's answer twice.

THE HIJACK BUCKET IS REPORTED SEPARATELY AND NOT FOLDED INTO THE HEADLINE,
because the prior Go typing attempt moved 692 edges and put 118 of them (17.1%)
onto the WRONG in-repo symbol. The 157 in-repo landings are type 84, function 62,
method 9, struct 1, field 1. The 84 `type` landings are Go type CONVERSIONS
(`caddy.Duration(x)`) -- calls only syntactically. That edge was already a `calls`
edge before this change, pointing at `external`; this makes its target accurate
and thereby makes a pre-existing modelling question visible. That question is
WI-jalal's family (a calls edge whose dst is not callable), not this one's.

2 of 13 repos changed by exactly zero (cosign, gocryptfs). That null is only
reportable because the positive control fires: a synthetic /v2 fixture moves 1
